<title>USA: Photo says knows no reason for stock rise.</title>
<headline>Photo says knows no reason for stock rise.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Photo Control Corp said it did not know why its stock was up one to 4-1/2 on 2,000 shares of trading volume.</p>
<p>&quot;Somebody must have just decided they wanted to buy some. Our stock is kind of thinly traded. So if somebody buys a few thousand shares, it can move,&quot; said president Les Willig.</p>
<p>Minneapolis-based Photo Control designs, makes and markets cameras, film and other photographics accessories.</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
